  "description": "Proposed replacement air conditioning unit, terraces, new windows and new first floor openings",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;Any new plant shall be installed, together with any associated ancillary equipment, so as to prevent the transmission of noise and vibration into neighbouring premises. The rated noise level from all plant and ancillary equipment shall not increase the existing background noise level (10dB below) when measured 1m external from the nearest residential or noise sensitive premises. An assessment of the expected noise levels shall be carried out by a suitably qualified (IOA accredited) and experienced acoustic consultant, in accordance with BS 4142:2014+A1:2019 ‘Methods for rating and assessing industrial and commercial sound,’ and any mitigation measures necessary to achieve the above required noise levels shall be submitted to the Local Planning Authority in writing for approval.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The plant shall thereafter be installed and maintained in accordance with the approved details.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To protect acceptable local noise levels.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;A post installation noise assessment noise report shall be submitted to the local planning authority that demonstrates that the predicted noise level of 36dBLAeq at 1m from the NSR1 and 30dBLAeq at 1m from the NSR2 are not being exceeded when the five Heat Recovery VRF units are being used simultaneously at any time, and in compliance with Condition 3.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To protect acceptable local noise levels.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
